  "conclusion": "These sampled static views do not establish a visual improvement or successful recovery of hidden grasp. Overall numerical self-motion remains above currentMP despite smoothing gains relative to raw. Some local intervals improve, and exact hidden finger pose or grasp timing remains unverified.",
  "limits": [
    "No continuous playback was performed by this reviewer. Adjacent snapshots permit a local pose comparison, not a full timing/lag or flicker assessment.",
    "The preview paints the full transparent human mesh without object-depth occlusion. Mesh shown across the table does not prove penetration.",
    "Generated geometric proposals are inferred values;21 admitted points do not imply visibility or calibrated confidence. Missing MP targets do not prove occlusion.",
    "MP comparisons are detector agreement, not ground-truth accuracy. Very small apparent palm width makes normalized2D opening ratios unstable.",
    "Both pooled20-joint-by-frame p95 and per-frame-mean-then-p95 are stored separately in the numerical receipt and must not be mixed. All motion metrics here are prediction-only, not official reference-relative ACC.",
    "Smoothing uses raw estimates across original holdout times before MHR fitting. Direct holdout fitting weights are zero, but generated smoothed holdout agreement is not independent.",
